# Linear GitHub magic words

Docs: [linear.app/docs/github#magic-words](https://linear.app/docs/github#magic-words)

A Linear key in parentheses (`(DEV-833)`), in the branch name, or late in a paragraph is **not** enough for commit linking. Linear needs a **magic word immediately before** `DEV-###`.

Put this on **its own line** (not buried in a sentence) in **both**:

1. The **commit subject or body**
2. The **PR title and/or description** (PR comments are ignored)

## Closing — this change fully resolves the issue

`close` `closes` `fix` `fixes` `resolve` `resolves` `complete` `completes` `implement` `implements` (and tense variants)

BeTaxed default when the PR should close the issue on merge:

```
Fixes DEV-833
```

Also valid: `Closes DEV-833`, `Resolves DEV-833`.

## Non-closing — partial / stacked work

`ref` `refs` `references` `part of` `contributes to` `toward` `towards`

```
Refs DEV-833
```

## Relation only

`relates to` `related to`

## Do not use

- **`Addresses DEV-###`** — not a Linear magic word
- Magic words only in a PR **comment**
- `skip DEV-###` / `ignore DEV-###` unless you intend to unlink

This is GitHub↔Linear automation. Do **not** set Linear workflow status via MCP (`linear-no-status-changes.mdc`).
